===== MILESTONE 1C COMPLETE =====
Saved results: /home/user4/alzheimers-thesis/reports/thesis_final/milestone_1c_selective_prediction_v1
No classifier retrained and no historical predictions modified.
Subject-bootstrap intervals are conditional; five CV repetitions are correlated.
Selection rankings are retrospective and use unlabeled held-out certainty scores.
Five-minute methods require 300 seconds of EEG and cannot make 60-second decisions.
Fractional tie weights avoid arbitrary selection among identical consensus scores.
